inference_trace:
Track the index of the most recent `1`. For each new `1` at index `i`, the number of zeros between it and the previous `1` is `i - last - 1`. If that gap is smaller than `k`, return `false`. If the scan finishes without a violation, return `true`.

This runs in O(n) time and O(1) extra space.

```cpp
class Solution {
public:
    bool kLengthApart(vector<int>& nums, int k) {
        int last = -1;
        for (int i = 0; i < (int)nums.size(); i++) {
            if (nums[i] == 1) {
                if (last != -1 && i - last - 1 < k) return false;
                last = i;
            }
        }
        return true;
    }
};
```

