Take the first two points as the reference line. Every other point must lie on that same line.

For each point `(x, y)`, use the cross-product test:

`(x1 - x0) * (y - y0) == (y1 - y0) * (x - x0)`

If this holds for all points, they are collinear. This avoids division, so vertical lines need no special case.

Coordinates are bounded by 10^4, so each difference is at most 2×10^4. Each product is at most 4×10^8, which fits in an `int`. I still use `long long` for safety.

```cpp
