inference_trace:
Find the largest candy count first. Kid `i` will have the greatest number of candies after receiving all the extras exactly when `candies[i] + extraCandies >= max`. Ties count as greatest, so the comparison uses `>=`.

This runs in O(n) time with one pass to find the maximum and one pass to build the result.

```cpp
class Solution {
public:
    vector<bool> kidsWithCandies(vector<int>& candies, int extraCandies) {
        int mx = *max_element(candies.begin(), candies.end());
        vector<bool> res;
        res.reserve(candies.size());
        for (int c : candies) res.push_back(c + extraCandies >= mx);
        return res;
    }
};
```

