inference_trace:
Mark every value in `nums` in a lookup array. Then walk the list once and count the nodes that end a component.

A node ends a component when:
- its value is in `nums`, and
- the next node is either null or has a value not in `nums`.

Since `0 <= Node.val < n <= 10^4`, a fixed boolean array of size 10001 is enough for the lookup. This gives O(n) time and O(n) extra space.

```cpp
class Solution {
public:
    int numComponents(ListNode* head, vector<int>& nums) {
        vector<bool> in(10001, false);
        for (int x : nums) in[x] = true;
        int cnt = 0;
        for (ListNode* p = head; p; p = p->next) {
            if (in[p->val] && (!p->next || !in[p->next->val])) cnt++;
        }
        return cnt;
    }
};
```

