inference_trace:
Use a bitmask DP over rows, where each mask records which seats in a row are occupied.

1. **Valid seats per row.** For row `i`, build `valid[i]` with bit `j` set when `seats[i][j] == '.'`.

2. **Which masks a row may use.** A mask `s` is allowed in row `i` when:
   - it only uses good seats: `(s & ~valid[i]) == 0`;
   - no two students sit side by side: `(s & (s << 1)) == 0`.

3. **Compatibility with the previous row.** A mask `s` can follow mask `p` when no student can see upper-left or upper-right:
   - `(s & (p << 1)) == 0`;
   - `(s & (p >> 1)) == 0`.

4. **Transition.** `dp[i][s] = max over compatible p of dp[i-1][p] + popcount(s)`. Masks that are invalid get `-1` so they are never used.

5. **Answer.** Take the maximum of `dp` over all masks of the last row.

**Complexity.** With `n ≤ 8` there are at most 256 masks, so each row costs at most 256 × 256 checks. Over 8 rows that is about 0.5M operations.

```cpp
class Solution {
public:
    int maxStudents(vector<vector<char>>& seats) {
        int m = seats.size(), n = seats[0].size();
        int full = 1 << n;
        vector<int> dp(full, -1), ndp(full);
        dp[0] = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < m; i++) {
            int valid = 0;
            for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) if (seats[i][j] == '.') valid |= 1 << j;
            fill(ndp.begin(), ndp.end(), -1);
            for (int s = 0; s < full; s++) {
                if (s & ~valid) continue;
                if (s & (s << 1)) continue;
                int c = __builtin_popcount(s);
                for (int p = 0; p < full; p++) {
                    if (dp[p] < 0) continue;
                    if ((s & (p << 1)) || (s & (p >> 1))) continue;
                    ndp[s] = max(ndp[s], dp[p] + c);
                }
            }
            swap(dp, ndp);
        }
        int ans = 0;
        for (int s = 0; s < full; s++) ans = max(ans, dp[s]);
        return ans;
    }
};
```

