inference_trace:
Sort the numbers in descending order and take the largest ones greedily. Stop as soon as the sum taken is strictly greater than the sum of what is left (`total - taken`).

Taking the largest elements first gives the smallest possible size. Among subsets of that size, it also gives the maximum sum. The result is already in non-increasing order because we picked from a descending sort.

```cpp
class Solution {
public:
    vector<int> minSubsequence(vector<int>& nums) {
        sort(nums.begin(), nums.end(), greater<int>());
        int total = 0;
        for (int x : nums) total += x;
        vector<int> res;
        int s = 0;
        for (int x : nums) {
            s += x;
            res.push_back(x);
            if (s > total - s) break;
        }
        return res;
    }
};
```

