Split each cell into 4 triangles and join connected pieces with union-find. The number of regions is the number of distinct roots at the end.

**Triangle labels.** For cell `(i, j)`, number its triangles as base index `4*(i*n + j)` plus:
- 0 = top
- 1 = right
- 2 = bottom
- 3 = left

**Unions inside a cell:**
- `' '`: union all four triangles (0, 1, 2, 3).
- `'/'`: the slash runs from top-right to bottom-left. Union top with left (0–3) and right with bottom (1–2).
- `'\'`: the slash runs from top-left to bottom-right. Union top with right (0–1) and bottom with left (2–3).

**Unions across cells:**
- The bottom of `(i, j)` meets the top of `(i+1, j)`.
- The right of `(i, j)` meets the left of `(i, j+1)`.

**Counting.** Start with `4*n*n` components and decrement the count on every successful union. The remaining count is the answer.

```cpp
class Solution {
public:
    vector<int> p;
    int cnt;
    int find(int x){ while(p[x]!=x){ p[x]=p[p[x]]; x=p[x]; } return x; }
    void unite(int a,int b){ a=find(a); b=find(b); if(a!=b){ p[a]=b; cnt--; } }
    int regionsBySlashes(vector<string>& grid) {
        int n = grid.size();
        p.resize(4*n*n);
        for(int i=0;i<4*n*n;i++) p[i]=i;
        cnt = 4*n*n;
        for(int i=0;i<n;i++){
            for(int j=0;j<n;j++){
                int b = 4*(i*n+j);
                char c = grid[i][j];
                if(c==' '){
                    unite(b,b+1); unite(b+1,b+2); unite(b+2,b+3);
                } else if(c=='/'){
                    unite(b,b+3); unite(b+1,b+2);
                } else {
                    unite(b,b+1); unite(b+2,b+3);
                }
                if(i+1<n) unite(b+2, 4*((i+1)*n+j));
                if(j+1<n) unite(b+1, 4*(i*n+j+1)+3);
            }
        }
        return cnt;
    }
};
```

