Approach: first count how many parentheses must be removed, then run a pruned DFS that removes exactly that many and collects the valid results.

1. **Count the minimum removals.** Scan left to right with a counter `l` of unmatched `(`.
   - On `(`, increment `l`.
   - On `)`, if `l > 0` decrement it; otherwise this `)` can never be matched, so increment `r`.
   - At the end, `l` unmatched `(` and `r` unmatched `)` must be removed. Together this is the minimum.

2. **DFS over positions** with state `(index, l, r, open, current string)`:
   - `open` is the number of `(` kept so far that are not yet closed.
   - **Remove** the current parenthesis if removals of that type remain (`l > 0` or `r > 0`).
   - **Keep** a `(` freely, which increments `open`.
   - **Keep** a `)` only if `open > 0`, which decrements `open`.
   - Letters are always kept.

3. **Collect results.** At the end of the string, accept the result if `l == 0`, `r == 0` and `open == 0`.

4. **Avoid duplicates.** Store results in a `set`. The input has at most 20 parentheses, so this is fine. Skipping runs of identical characters would be an optional optimization.

```cpp
class Solution {
public:
    set<string> res;
    string s;
    void dfs(int i, int l, int r, int open, string& cur) {
        if (i == (int)s.size()) {
            if (l == 0 && r == 0 && open == 0) res.insert(cur);
            return;
        }
        char c = s[i];
        if (c == '(') {
            if (l > 0) dfs(i + 1, l - 1, r, open, cur);
            cur.push_back(c);
            dfs(i + 1, l, r, open + 1, cur);
            cur.pop_back();
        } else if (c == ')') {
            if (r > 0) dfs(i + 1, l, r - 1, open, cur);
            if (open > 0) {
                cur.push_back(c);
                dfs(i + 1, l, r, open - 1, cur);
                cur.pop_back();
            }
        } else {
            cur.push_back(c);
            dfs(i + 1, l, r, open, cur);
            cur.pop_back();
        }
    }
    vector<string> removeInvalidParentheses(string s) {
        this->s = s;
        int l = 0, r = 0;
        for (char c : s) {
            if (c == '(') l++;
            else if (c == ')') {
                if (l > 0) l--;
                else r++;
            }
        }
        string cur;
        dfs(0, l, r, 0, cur);
        return vector<string>(res.begin(), res.end());
    }
};
```

