If the string is empty, no steps are needed. Otherwise there are only two cases:

- **The string is already a palindrome.** Remove the whole string in one step, so the answer is 1.
- **The string is not a palindrome.** Remove all the `'a'` characters as one subsequence; it is a palindrome because every character is the same. Then remove all the `'b'` characters the same way. That takes 2 steps.

So the answer is never more than 2, and checking whether `s` is a palindrome is enough.

```cpp
class Solution {
public:
    int removePalindromeSub(string s) {
        if (s.empty()) return 0;
        int i = 0, j = (int)s.size() - 1;
        while (i < j) {
            if (s[i] != s[j]) return 2;
            i++; j--;
        }
        return 1;
    }
};
```

