inference_trace:
Sort the products lexicographically. All products sharing a given prefix then sit in one contiguous block of the sorted list.

For each prefix of `searchWord`:
1. Use `lower_bound` to find the first product that is not less than the prefix.
2. Starting from that position, check up to 3 consecutive products.
3. Add each one that starts with the prefix; stop at the first one that doesn't, since no later product can match.

Because each new prefix is lexicographically at least as large as the previous one, the search can begin from the previous start position.

```cpp
class Solution {
public:
    vector<vector<string>> suggestedProducts(vector<string>& products, string searchWord) {
        sort(products.begin(), products.end());
        vector<vector<string>> res;
        string prefix;
        auto start = products.begin();
        for (char c : searchWord) {
            prefix += c;
            start = lower_bound(start, products.end(), prefix);
            vector<string> cur;
            for (auto it = start; it != products.end() && cur.size() < 3; ++it) {
                if (it->compare(0, prefix.size(), prefix) == 0) cur.push_back(*it);
                else break;
            }
            res.push_back(cur);
        }
        return res;
    }
};
```

