Track the longest duration seen so far and the key that produced it, scanning the presses in order:

1. Start with the first keypress: its duration is `releaseTimes[0]` and its key is `keysPressed[0]`.
2. For each later index `i`, the duration is `releaseTimes[i] - releaseTimes[i-1]`.
3. Replace the current answer if this duration is strictly longer, or if it ties and the key is lexicographically larger.

This runs in O(n) time with O(1) extra space.

```cpp
class Solution {
public:
    char slowestKey(vector<int>& releaseTimes, string keysPressed) {
        int best = releaseTimes[0];
        char ans = keysPressed[0];
        for (size_t i = 1; i < releaseTimes.size(); i++) {
            int d = releaseTimes[i] - releaseTimes[i-1];
            if (d > best || (d == best && keysPressed[i] > ans)) {
                best = d;
                ans = keysPressed[i];
            }
        }
        return ans;
    }
};
```

