Values are small (1 to 50), so instead of scanning all ancestors we can track, for each value, the deepest ancestor holding it.

**Approach**

1. Precompute `cop[v]`: the list of values `w` in 1..50 with `gcd(v, w) == 1`.
2. Run an iterative DFS from node 0. An explicit stack avoids recursion-depth problems, since `n` can be up to 10^5.
3. For each value `v`, keep a stack `st[v]` of `(depth, node)` pairs for ancestors on the current root-to-node path whose value is `v`.
4. When entering node `u`:
   - Look at every value `w` in `cop[nums[u]]`.
   - If `st[w]` is non-empty, its top is the deepest ancestor with value `w`.
   - Among these tops, take the one with the greatest depth as `ans[u]`; if none exist, `ans[u] = -1`.
   - Then push `(depth, u)` onto `st[nums[u]]`.
5. When leaving node `u`, pop from `st[nums[u]]`.

**Iterative DFS details**

- Each stack frame stores `(node, parent, depth, edge-iterator index)`.
- When a node is first pushed, compute its answer and push it onto its value stack.
- Advance the iterator through neighbors, skipping the parent.
- When all neighbors are done, pop the node from its value stack and from the DFS stack.

**Complexity**

Each node checks at most 50 values, so the total time is O(50·n).

```cpp
class Solution {
public:
    vector<int> getCoprimes(vector<int>& nums, vector<vector<int>>& edges) {
        int n = nums.size();
        vector<vector<int>> adj(n);
        for (auto& e : edges) {
            adj[e[0]].push_back(e[1]);
            adj[e[1]].push_back(e[0]);
        }
        vector<vector<int>> cop(51);
        for (int a = 1; a <= 50; a++)
            for (int b = 1; b <= 50; b++)
                if (std::gcd(a, b) == 1) cop[a].push_back(b);
        vector<vector<pair<int,int>>> st(51);
        vector<int> ans(n, -1);
        // frame: node, parent, depth, idx
        struct F { int u, p, d, i; };
        vector<F> stk;
        auto enter = [&](int u, int d) {
            int best = -1, bd = -1;
            for (int w : cop[nums[u]]) {
                if (!st[w].empty() && st[w].back().first > bd) {
                    bd = st[w].back().first;
                    best = st[w].back().second;
                }
            }
            ans[u] = best;
            st[nums[u]].push_back({d, u});
        };
        enter(0, 0);
        stk.push_back({0, -1, 0, 0});
        while (!stk.empty()) {
            F& f = stk.back();
            if (f.i < (int)adj[f.u].size()) {
                int v = adj[f.u][f.i++];
                if (v == f.p) continue;
                int d = f.d + 1;
                int u = f.u;
                enter(v, d);
                stk.push_back({v, u, d, 0});
            } else {
                st[nums[f.u]].pop_back();
                stk.pop_back();
            }
        }
        return ans;
    }
};
```

