inference_trace:
A word is uncommon exactly when it appears once in the combined text of both sentences:
- If it appears once in total, it is in one sentence only, once.
- If it appears more than once in total, it either repeats within one sentence or shows up in both, so it is not uncommon.

So the approach is:
1. Split both sentences into words.
2. Count every word's occurrences in a hash map.
3. Return the words whose count is 1.

```cpp
class Solution {
public:
    vector<string> uncommonFromSentences(string s1, string s2) {
        unordered_map<string, int> cnt;
        istringstream iss(s1 + " " + s2);
        string w;
        while (iss >> w) cnt[w]++;
        vector<string> res;
        for (auto& p : cnt) if (p.second == 1) res.push_back(p.first);
        return res;
    }
};
```

